(You will rejoice to hear that no disaster has accompanied the) Tj
T*
(commencement of an enterprise which you have regarded with such evil) Tj
T*
(forebodings. I arrived here yesterday, and my first task is to assure) Tj
T*
(my dear sister of my welfare and increasing confidence in the success) Tj
T*
(of my undertaking.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(I am already far north of London, and as I walk in the streets of) Tj
T*
(Petersburgh, I feel a cold northern breeze play upon my cheeks, which) Tj
T*
(braces my nerves and fills me with delight. Do you understand this) Tj
T*
(feeling? This breeze, which has travelled from the regions towards) Tj
T*
(which I am advancing, gives me a foretaste of those icy climes.) Tj
T*
(Inspirited by this wind of promise, my daydreams become more fervent) Tj
T*
(and vivid. I try in vain to be persuaded that the pole is the seat of) Tj
T*
(frost and desolation; it ever presents itself to my imagination as the) Tj
T*
(region of beauty and delight. There, Margaret, the sun is for ever) Tj
T*
(visible, its broad disk just skirting the horizon and diffusing a) Tj
T*
(perpetual splendour. There-for with your leave, my sister, I will put) Tj
T*
(some trust in preceding navigators-there snow and frost are banished;) Tj
T*
(and, sailing over a calm sea, we may be wafted to a land surpassing in) Tj
T*
(wonders and in beauty every region hitherto discovered on the habitable) Tj
T*
(globe. Its productions and features may be without example, as the) Tj
T*
(phenomena of the heavenly bodies undoubtedly are in those undiscovered) Tj
T*
(solitudes. What may not be expected in a country of eternal light? I) Tj
T*
(may there discover the wondrous power which attracts the needle and may) Tj
T*
(regulate a thousand celestial observations that require only this) Tj
T*
(voyage to render their seeming eccentricities consistent for ever. I) Tj
T*
(shall satiate my ardent curiosity with the sight of a part of the world) Tj
T*
(never before visited, and may tread a land never before imprinted by) Tj
T*
(the foot of man. These are my enticements, and they are sufficient to) Tj
T*
(conquer all fear of danger or death and to induce me to commence this) Tj
T*
(laborious voyage with the joy a child feels when he embarks in a little) Tj
T*
(boat, with his holiday mates, on an expedition of discovery up his) Tj
T*
(native river. But supposing all these conjectures to be false, you) Tj
T*
(cannot contest the inestimable benefit which I shall confer on all) Tj
T*
(mankind, to the last generation, by discovering a passage near the pole) Tj
T*
(to those countries, to reach which at present so many months are) Tj
T*
(requisite; or by ascertaining the secret of the magnet, which, if at) Tj
T*
(all possible, can only be effected by an undertaking such as mine.) Tj
